    "explanation": "A non-rebreather mask (NRB) at 10–15 L/min delivers up to 90% FiO2 because the one-way valves prevent exhaled air from re-entering the reservoir bag. A simple face mask delivers 35–50% at 6–10 L/min, a nasal cannula 24–44% at 1–6 L/min, and a Venturi mask provides precise but lower concentrations. For a spontaneously breathing patient, only a BVM connected to 100% O2 exceeds the NRB, but BVM requires a provider to squeeze it. The NRB is the highest-output device used without active ventilation.",
