        "isCorrect": true,
        "order": 1,
        "explanation": "Correct. Chronic hypercapnic COPD patients may breathe primarily in response to low O2 rather than high CO2. Excess oxygen can blunt this drive. Brady Ch.13 specifies 88–92% for these patients."
