    "caseOutcome": "Agitation and diaphoresis after naloxone in an opioid-dependent user is precipitated withdrawal — a documented, expected adverse effect. Per NAEMSP 2017, this confirms treatment was successful (respirations restored) but requires scene safety measures and transport for monitoring.",
