    "sourceRef": "Simons FER et al. WAO 2011 Anaphylaxis Guidelines; Brady Emergency Care 14th Ed — Ch.25; NEMSES 2021",
    "explanation": "Biphasic anaphylaxis occurs in ~5% of cases — a second phase of symptoms 1–72 hours after initial resolution. If symptoms return within the same encounter, the correct action is a second dose of epinephrine 0.3 mg IM. There is no maximum number of epinephrine doses in anaphylaxis — repeat every 5–15 minutes if symptoms recur or are not adequately controlled. Antihistamines (diphenhydramine) DO NOT reverse anaphylaxis — they are adjunct only and work too slowly.",
    "difficulty": 3,
    "tags": [
      "epinephrine",
      "anaphylaxis",
      "biphasic",
      "repeat-dose"
    ],
