    "explanation": "The 5 rights: (1) Right PATIENT — confirm identity, consent, contraindications; (2) Right MEDICATION — correct drug, not similar-sounding; (3) Right DOSE — appropriate amount and concentration; (4) Right ROUTE — oral/IM/SL/inhaled as prescribed; (5) Right TIME — indicated now, not already given recently. Some sources add (6) Right Documentation. In prehospital care, EMTs must verify all 5 rights before ANY medication administration — including assisting with patient-prescribed medications. This framework prevents the most common medication errors: wrong drug, wrong dose, wrong patient.",
