        "id": "respiratory-emergencies-024-2",
        "text": "The endotracheal tube is in the oesophagus",
        "isCorrect": false,
        "order": 3,
        "explanation": "If ETCO₂ is consistently low but shows any waveform, oesophageal intubation is less likely — oesophageal placement typically shows no waveform or returns to baseline rapidly. Very low ETCO₂ during CPR reflects poor perfusion."
