    "explanation": "Each suction attempt should last no more than 15 seconds in adults (10 seconds in children, 5 seconds in infants). Prolonged suctioning removes oxygen along with secretions and can cause vagally-mediated bradycardia. Pre-oxygenate before suctioning, suction on withdrawal (not insertion), and monitor SpO₂ and heart rate throughout.",
