    "explanation": "Gurgling = fluid in the upper airway (blood, vomit, secretions). This requires immediate suctioning to prevent aspiration. Position the patient appropriately (turn to the side if possible without spinal precautions), suction with a rigid Yankauer catheter, and provide supplemental oxygen. Aspiration of gastric contents causes severe aspiration pneumonitis.",
