    "sourceRef": "Weaver 2014, NEJM — Hyperbaric Oxygen for CO Poisoning; Brady 14th Ed Ch. 31",
    "explanation": "CO poisoning treatment: 100% oxygen via tight-fitting non-rebreather mask at 15 L/min. High-concentration O₂ accelerates COHb dissociation — at room air, COHb half-life is ~300 min; at 100% O₂, it drops to ~60–80 min; hyperbaric O₂ (100% at 3 atm) reduces it to ~20 min. NRB at 15 L/min is the highest prehospital O₂ delivery for spontaneously breathing patients. Never use NC or simple mask — maximum FiO₂ is essential.",
