    "text": "An EMT is assisting a patient with their prescribed albuterol MDI. After confirming the five rights and checking for contraindications, what is the correct sequence?",
    "questionStyle": "standard",
    "caseContext": "",
    "caseOutcome": "",
    "sourceRef": "Brady Emergency Care 14th Ed, Ch. 16; NEMSES 2021 — EMT Assisted Medications",
    "explanation": "Correct MDI technique: shake well × 5–6 times, patient exhales fully, place mouthpiece in mouth (or use spacer), actuate during slow deep inhalation (simultaneously), patient holds breath 10 seconds to maximise airway deposition, then exhales. Wait 1 minute between puffs. Coordinate actuation with inhalation — the most common source of error.",
    "difficulty": 2,
