    "explanation": "Increasing ventilation resistance + absent left breath sounds + tracheal deviation (late sign) = tension pneumothorax until proven otherwise. Air accumulates under pressure in the pleural space, collapsing the ipsilateral lung and shifting the mediastinum. BVM resistance increases as compliance worsens. This is a life-threatening emergency requiring immediate needle decompression (2nd ICS, MCL, or 4th/5th ICS, MAL). Do not wait for a chest X-ray.",
    "difficulty": 3,
