    "text": "A patient in respiratory arrest has no gag reflex. You insert an oropharyngeal airway (OPA) and begin BVM ventilation. After 2 breaths, the patient's stomach is visibly distending. What is the most likely cause and correction?",
    "questionStyle": "case-based",
    "caseContext": "Adult patient in respiratory arrest. OPA inserted, BVM ventilation attempted. After 2 breaths: abdomen visibly rises and falls rather than the chest, gurgling heard over the epigastrium.",
