    "explanation": "BE-FAST: Balance (sudden loss of balance or coordination), Eyes (sudden vision loss or double vision), Face (facial droop — ask patient to smile), Arm (arm drift or weakness — ask patient to raise both arms), Speech (slurred, strange, or absent speech), Time (call 911 immediately and note last known well time). The BE addition to FAST improves stroke identification sensitivity from 79% to 95% (Aroor et al., 2017).",
    "difficulty": 1,
