    "explanation": "Last known well (LKW) time is the most critical data point for stroke management. It determines eligibility for thrombolysis (tPA window: 3–4.5 hours from onset) and mechanical thrombectomy (up to 24 hours in select patients). Pre-notification to the stroke centre while en route reduces door-to-needle time. Transport to the stroke centre bypassing the closer non-stroke hospital is appropriate per protocol.",
