    "explanation": "This is the postictal state — the recovery period following a seizure characterised by confusion, lethargy, unresponsiveness, and possible focal neurological deficits (Todd's paralysis). Expected duration: 5-30 minutes, variable. Management: lateral recumbent position to maintain airway and allow secretion drainage, supplemental O2 if SpO2 <94%, suction if needed, do not restrain. Monitor for prolonged postictal state (>30 min), which warrants concern for status epilepticus, stroke, or intracranial pathology.",
