    "explanation": "Resolution of focal neurological deficits after glucose administration confirms hypoglycaemia as the cause. However, the patient must still be transported for hospital evaluation because: (1) the underlying cause of hypoglycaemia must be identified; (2) BGL must be monitored (rebound hypoglycaemia); (3) neurological deficits that resolved may recur; (4) hypoglycaemia itself can cause permanent neuronal injury if severe. Do not release the patient on scene.",
