    "caseOutcome": "First seizures in previously healthy individuals require hospital evaluation to identify underlying cause (structural lesion, metabolic disorder, idiopathic epilepsy). The likelihood of a structural cause (tumour, AVM) in a first seizure requires MRI — this cannot be excluded prehospitally. Most first seizures in young adults are idiopathic, but all require workup.",
