    "explanation": "Any first seizure requires hospital evaluation to identify: structural causes (tumour, AVM, abscess), metabolic causes (hyponatraemia, hypoglycaemia, uraemia), infection (encephalitis, meningitis), and to determine whether anti-epileptic therapy should be started. ACEP 2014 guidelines recommend imaging and specialist referral for all first unprovoked seizures regardless of clinical recovery.",
