    "explanation": "U = Uraemia (kidney failure). Uraemia causes AMS through accumulation of nitrogenous waste products that are normally cleared by functional kidneys. Prehospital significance: recognise that renal failure can cause AMS in dialysis patients who miss sessions, or in dehydrated/septic patients with acute kidney injury. Look for: history of kidney disease, dialysis access (fistulas), decreased urine output, signs of volume overload. No specific prehospital treatment — supportive care and transport.",
    "difficulty": 3,
