    "text": "What is the normal fasting blood glucose range in a healthy adult?",
    "questionStyle": "standard",
    "caseContext": "",
    "caseOutcome": "",
    "sourceRef": "ADA Standards of Medical Care 2023, Section 2 — Classification and Diagnosis",
    "explanation": "Normal fasting plasma glucose: 70–99 mg/dL (3.9–5.5 mmol/L). Pre-diabetes: 100–125 mg/dL (impaired fasting glucose). Diabetes: ≥126 mg/dL on two occasions. Hypoglycaemia symptoms typically begin below 70 mg/dL in non-diabetic patients; in brittle diabetics, symptoms may occur at higher levels due to adapted baseline.",
    "difficulty": 1,
    "tags": [
      "blood-glucose",
      "normal-values",
      "diabetes",
      "assessment"
    ],
    "nremtDomain": "SECONDARY_ASSESSMENT",
