    "explanation": "The 15-15 rule: give 15g of rapid-acting carbohydrate (glucose gel, juice, glucose tablets), then recheck blood glucose after 15 minutes. If still <70 mg/dL and patient remains symptomatic, repeat the 15g dose. If glucose rises to ≥70 mg/dL and symptoms resolve, provide a small mixed snack to maintain levels.",
