    "explanation": "Blood glucose should be checked in ANY patient with: altered level of consciousness, seizure (new onset or breakthrough), suspected stroke, cardiac arrest, behavioural disturbance, or unexplained syncope. Hypoglycaemia mimics and can cause all these presentations. Missing hypoglycaemia in a 'stroke' patient delays the simple and curative treatment.",
