    "explanation": "Sulfonylureas (glipizide, glyburide, glimepiride) stimulate insulin secretion for up to 24 hours regardless of blood glucose level. This causes prolonged, recurrent hypoglycaemia. Even after treating with glucose, the sulfonylurea continues driving insulin secretion → re-hypoglycaemia. All sulfonylurea-induced hypoglycaemia patients require hospital admission for monitoring — do not leave at home regardless of initial glucose response.",
