    "caseContext": "",
    "caseOutcome": "",
    "sourceRef": "ADA Standards of Medical Care 2023 — Technology; Brady Emergency Care 14th Ed, Ch. 29",
    "explanation": "Insulin pumps deliver continuous rapid-acting insulin. A pump malfunction, kink in the tubing, or programming error can cause severe, prolonged hypoglycaemia or DKA. If accessible, the insulin pump should be turned off/suspended to stop ongoing insulin delivery. This prevents continued insulin delivery while glucose is being corrected. Inform the receiving hospital team about the pump.",
