    "explanation": "Type 1 DM: autoimmune destruction of pancreatic beta cells → absolute insulin deficiency → cannot survive without exogenous insulin → DKA risk is high when insulin is missed. Type 2 DM: insulin resistance + progressive relative insulin deficiency; managed with lifestyle, oral agents, and eventually insulin. T1DM patients who miss insulin can develop DKA rapidly. T2DM patients have residual insulin production — more resistant to DKA but can develop HHS.",
