    "explanation": "Sulphonylureas (glipizide, glyburide, glimepiride) stimulate pancreatic insulin secretion independently of blood glucose — continuing to release insulin even as BGL drops. This creates prolonged, recurrent hypoglycaemia requiring repeated glucose or IV dextrose infusion for 12–24 hours. Patients on sulphonylureas MUST be transported and monitored in hospital — sending home after correction is dangerous. Metformin has very low hypoglycaemia risk.",
