    "sourceRef": "Brady Emergency Care 14th Ed — Ch.15, 29; AHA 2020 BLS Guidelines",
    "explanation": "Glucagon IM commonly causes nausea and vomiting. An unconscious or semi-conscious patient who vomits is at aspiration risk. Correct positioning: recovery position (lateral decubitus) — allows vomit to drain from the mouth. Suction should be immediately available. Never leave an unconscious patient supine without constant airway monitoring.",
    "difficulty": 1,
