    "explanation": "Blood glucose measurement is the definitive prehospital differentiator. Both hypoglycaemia and stroke can cause: confusion, slurred speech, focal weakness, facial droop. BGL <70 mg/dL in an AMS patient is hypoglycaemia until proven otherwise — treat and reassess. If deficits resolve after correction: hypoglycaemia was the cause. Persistent deficits after correction: stroke or combined pathology. All AMS patients with focal deficits should have BGL checked and be transported.",
