    "explanation": "Priority system involvement in anaphylaxis: (1) Airway/respiratory — stridor indicates upper airway angioedema; can cause fatal asphyxiation within minutes. (2) Cardiovascular — BP 72/40 is anaphylactic shock; distributive mechanism from histamine-mediated vasodilation. (3) Skin — urticaria is alarming but not immediately fatal. Epinephrine addresses all three simultaneously.",
    "difficulty": 3,
