    "sourceRef": "WAO 2011; Brady Emergency Care 14th Ed, Ch. 32; ACAAI 2015",
    "explanation": "After epinephrine IM: reassess vital signs, symptom severity, and airway within 5 minutes. If insufficient improvement by 5–10 minutes, consider a second epinephrine dose. Continuous monitoring throughout transport: SpO₂, HR, BP, respiratory rate, skin findings. Epinephrine's duration of action is 20–30 minutes — ongoing monitoring detects biphasic reaction or early return of symptoms.",
    "difficulty": 2,
    "tags": [
      "reassessment",
      "epinephrine",
      "monitoring",
      "anaphylaxis",
      "allergy"
    ],
