    "explanation": "ALL anaphylaxis patients must be transported and observed in hospital for a minimum of 4–6 hours (WAO 2011 recommends 4–8 hours for uncomplicated cases). Reasons: (1) Biphasic anaphylaxis occurs in ~5% of patients — a second phase of symptoms 1–72 hours after initial resolution (Simons 2010 JACI); (2) Epinephrine's duration is 30–90 minutes — re-narcotisation risk analogous to naloxone; (3) Protracted anaphylaxis — some reactions require ongoing treatment. Risk factors for biphasic: severe initial reaction, delayed epinephrine, idiopathic trigger. Patients must never be discharged from scene even if fully recovered.",
