    "explanation": "Exercise-induced anaphylaxis (EIA): a form of anaphylaxis triggered by physical exertion. May be pure (any exercise) or food-dependent (specific food + exercise together — cofactor anaphylaxis). Presentation: occurs during or immediately after exercise; urticaria, angioedema, and cardiovascular collapse as in classic anaphylaxis. Important features: symptoms resolve with cessation of exercise if caught early; may recur on same day; often underdiagnosed as 'heat exhaustion' or 'overexertion.' Prehospital: treat identically with epinephrine IM. Stopping exercise immediately is the first step if symptoms begin during activity.",
    "difficulty": 3,
    "tags": [
      "exercise-induced-anaphylaxis",
      "cofactor",
      "physical-exertion"
    ],
