    "explanation": "Refractory laryngeal angioedema is a surgical airway emergency: (1) Repeat epinephrine 0.3 mg IM immediately (no maximum in anaphylaxis with recurrent symptoms); (2) Request ALS immediately for needle cricothyrotomy or surgical airway; (3) Attempt BVM ventilation with high O2; (4) Rapid transport to surgical emergency department. If BVM fails due to complete obstruction: needle cricothyrotomy may be within ALS scope. Epinephrine alone may not fully reverse established laryngeal oedema — progressive airway closure requires surgical backup.",
    "difficulty": 4,
