    "sourceRef": "Brady Emergency Care 14th Ed — Ch.30 Poisoning and Overdose",
    "explanation": "CO poisoning progresses predictably with increasing COHb levels: headache (COHb ~10–20%) → nausea and vomiting (~20–30%) → confusion and impaired judgment (~30–40%) → seizures (~40–50%) → coma and cardiovascular collapse (>50%). Brady Ch.30 presents this progression as the clinical framework for assessing severity.",
