    "explanation": "MUDPILES (Methanol, Uraemia, DKA, Propylene glycol, Isoniazid/Iron, Lactic acidosis, Ethylene glycol, Salicylates) is the mnemonic for causes of high anion gap metabolic acidosis. Toxic alcohols (methanol, ethylene glycol) are the most relevant EMS toxins in this group. Prehospital: supportive care, high-flow O2, IV access, and rapid transport — specific antidotes (fomepizole, ethanol, haemodialysis) are hospital-based. EMTs recognise AMS + suspected alcohol exposure as potentially toxic alcohol ingestion.",
    "difficulty": 4,
