        "text": "Upwind positioning is unnecessary for colourless gases because they cannot travel with the wind",
        "isCorrect": false,
        "order": 3,
        "explanation": "Incorrect. All gases travel with air currents regardless of colour. CO, hydrogen cyanide, and chlorine are all colourless and all travel downwind. Upwind positioning is critical for colourless gases."
