    "explanation": "APGAR: A=Appearance (colour), P=Pulse (HR), G=Grimace (reflex irritability), A=Activity (tone), R=Respiration. Each scored 0–2, total 0–10. Assessed at 1 and 5 minutes post-birth. 7–10=normal; 4–6=moderate concern; 0–3=immediate resuscitation. NRP note: do not wait for the 1-minute APGAR to begin resuscitation — start NRP if the neonate is not vigorous.",
