    "text": "In the management of croup, which of the following interventions is CONTRAINDICATED in the prehospital setting?",
    "questionStyle": "standard",
    "caseContext": "",
    "caseOutcome": "",
    "sourceRef": "Brady Emergency Care 14th Ed — Ch.38 Paediatric Emergencies; NEMSES 2021 — EMT Instructional Guidelines, Paediatric Emergencies Ch.14",
    "explanation": "Direct laryngoscopy is absolutely contraindicated in the prehospital management of croup. Attempting to examine or instrument the airway can agitate the child, worsen laryngospasm, and precipitate complete obstruction. Prehospital management is calm reassurance, keep the child with the caregiver, humidified oxygen, and transport.",
    "difficulty": 3,
