    "questionStyle": "case-based",
    "caseContext": "You respond to a 2-year-old male with a 2-day history of upper respiratory infection. The mother reports he developed a harsh, barking cough this evening and has a rectal temperature of 38.2°C. On arrival the child is sitting in his mother's lap, mildly anxious, with audible inspiratory stridor at rest and mild intercostal retractions. He is pink, has good tone, and can be partially consoled by his mother. SpO₂ is 95% on room air.",
