    "explanation": "The gradual onset, barking cough, inspiratory stridor, low-grade fever, and mild distress in a 2-year-old are classic for croup (laryngotracheobronchitis). Prehospital management is calm reassurance with the caregiver, humidified blow-by oxygen, upright positioning, and transport. Direct examination of the throat or agitation is contraindicated.",
