    "caseContext": "A 9-year-old male was stung by a bee while playing on the school field. Approximately 8 minutes later he complains of throat tightening and difficulty swallowing. He has hives across his trunk and arms, periorbital oedema, and a hoarse voice. SpO₂ is 94% on room air. He is alert but visibly frightened. The school has a student-specific epinephrine auto-injector (EpiPen) prescribed to him in the nurse's office.",
