    "explanation": "This child has anaphylaxis — airway involvement (throat tightening, hoarse voice), skin signs (hives, oedema), and hypoxia (SpO₂ 94%) following a bee sting. The immediate first step is epinephrine administration — either assisting the patient with his prescribed auto-injector or administering per protocol. Epinephrine IM to the anterolateral thigh is the treatment of choice. Oxygen is administered simultaneously.",
