    "caseOutcome": "",
    "sourceRef": "DOT Emergency Response Guidebook 2024 Edition; Brady Emergency Care 14th Ed — Ch.51 HazMat",
    "explanation": "The Emergency Response Guidebook (ERG), published by the U.S. DOT, provides initial isolation and protective action distances for hazardous materials emergencies. Responders look up the 4-digit UN/NA number on the placard or shipping papers to find the appropriate guide page. The ERG provides initial isolation distances, protective action distances, and basic response guidance for the first 30 minutes of a hazmat response.",
    "difficulty": 2,
