  {
    "id": "ems-operations-050",
    "moduleSlug": "ems-operations",
    "text": "A GREEN-tagged patient at an MCI subsequently deteriorates — he is now unresponsive and apnoeic. What is the correct action?",
    "questionStyle": "case-based",
    "caseContext": "During an MCI with 22 patients, a 55-year-old male was initially tagged GREEN (walking wounded) with a minor ankle injury and directed to the casualty collection point. 15 minutes later a bystander alerts you that the patient has collapsed and is unresponsive. On reassessment: apnoeic after airway repositioning, carotid pulse present.",
    "caseOutcome": "The patient was immediately re-triaged to RED, airway was opened and maintained, and he was moved to the treatment area for immediate intervention. ALS was directed to the patient. He was found to be in ventricular fibrillation — defibrillation achieved ROSC. The patient had an undetected inferior STEMI. He survived to hospital discharge.",
    "sourceRef": "NEMSES 2021 — EMT Instructional Guidelines, MCI Ch.15; Brady Emergency Care 14th Ed — Ch.48",
    "explanation": "Triage is a dynamic process — patients must be re-triaged when their condition changes. This patient deteriorated from GREEN to RED (apnoeic with pulse). At an MCI, resources permit re-triage and re-categorisation. In adult MCI (START), a patient apnoeic after airway repositioning is BLACK — however, a pulse is present, and this patient was NOT initially assessed as apnoeic; he was ambulatory. This represents a new clinical deterioration. Re-triage to RED with immediate care is appropriate when conditions and resources allow.",
    "difficulty": 4,
    "tags": [
      "START-triage",
      "MCI",
      "re-triage",
      "dynamic-triage",
      "case-based",
      "deterioration"
    ],
    "nremtDomain": "OPERATIONS",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "ems-operations-050-0",
        "text": "Immediately re-triage to RED and direct available resources to the patient",
        "isCorrect": true,
        "order": 1,
        "explanation": "Triage is dynamic — a patient who deteriorates must be re-triaged. This patient has new critical findings requiring immediate reassignment to RED."
      },
      {
        "id": "ems-operations-050-1",
        "text": "Maintain GREEN tag — the original triage decision cannot be changed",
        "isCorrect": false,
        "order": 2,
        "explanation": "Triage is not static — conditions change and patients must be re-triaged when they deteriorate or improve."
      },
      {
        "id": "ems-operations-050-2",
        "text": "Tag BLACK immediately because he is apnoeic with pulse and no rescue breaths were given",
        "isCorrect": false,
        "order": 3,
        "explanation": "In adult START, apnoea after repositioning = BLACK, but this patient has a carotid pulse and this is a new deterioration from a known ambulatory patient — clinical judgment and re-triage to RED is appropriate, especially with available ALS resources."
      },
      {
        "id": "ems-operations-050-3",
        "text": "Direct another walking wounded patient to monitor him while you continue triage",
        "isCorrect": false,
        "order": 4,
        "explanation": "An unresponsive apnoeic patient requires trained EMS management, not bystander observation."
      }
    ]
  }
